    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.hues\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nmini.hues is not highlighting keywords like `local` and `function` in lua.\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f2e6f9a6-1c46-4f8f-a12a-859eb0bbb651)\r\n\r\n### Neovim version\r\n\r\nNVIM v0.11.0-dev-632+g33464189b\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n1. Just install mini.hues\r\n2. Run command `colorscheme randomhue`\r\n3. You can see that `local` and `function` keyowords are not highlighted.\r\n\r\n\r\n### Expected behavior\r\n\r\nThese keywords to be highlighted.\r\n\r\n### Actual behavior\r\n\r\nThese keywords are not highlighted.",
    "closed_at": "2024-08-18T17:57:52Z",
