            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "They should be highlighted as bold with \"normal\" foreground. If this is with enabled tree-sitter highlighting (which looks like it), then these words are highlighted with `@keyword` highlight group. It links to `Keyword`, which links to `Statement` which [is bold with normal foreground](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/d6e6a6fb010cc452b491704aa9ecc96a8aa2cde1/lua/mini/hues.lua#L543).\r\n\r\nDoes executing `:Inspect` on `local` (or any other word which you think is not highlighted) show `@keyword.lua links to Statement`)?\r\nIf yes, what does `:hi Statement` show? It should contain something like `cterm=bold gui=bold`.\r\nIf yes, then it is probably because bold font is configured to be the same as the normal font. 'mini.hues' relies on bold attribute quite a lot, so it is better to have it set up if you want to use 'mini.hues'.",
